# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Secrets and local state
# `.env` holds real local values. `.env.example` is the tracked template and is
# deliberately re-included so a fresh clone has every documented variable to fill in.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
.env
.env.*
!.env.example

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Python
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
*.egg-info/
.venv/
venv/

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Build output and tooling artifacts — all regenerable, none of them source.
# The tracked/ignored sets are recorded in docs/repository.md.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
build/
dist/
*.whl
.coverage
.coverage.*
htmlcov/
coverage.xml
.pytest_cache/
.mypy_cache/
.ruff_cache/

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Editors and OS
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
.idea/
.vscode/
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db
Desktop.ini
*.swp
*.swo
*~

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Documentation tree — all of docs/ stays local (operator decision 2026-10-26).
# Tickets, ADRs, spec, verification and the source runbooks are project working
# notes, not shipped product. Keep the repo to the core system only.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
docs/

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Agent configuration — dev-tool scaffolds that must never enter the repo.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
AGENTS.md
agents.md
CLAUDE.md
.claude/
.cursor/
